T Mechanism demo: motor, gears, string, band, ball
# Every element the physics engine knows, in one rig small enough to build.
# Note the feet: two posts in parallel planes can only be tied together through 3D connector pairs.
! two triangular posts, in the planes x = -2 and x = +2
C LB B7 -2,-2,0.5 x y
C LB2 B7 -2,-2,0.5 y x
C LF B7 -2,2,0.5 x y
C LF2 B7 -2,2,0.5 y x
C LT W8 -2,0,2.5 x y
R LB LF
R LB LT
R LF LT
C RB B7 2,-2,0.5 x y
C RB2 B7 2,-2,0.5 y x
C RF B7 2,2,0.5 x y
C RF2 B7 2,2,0.5 y x
C RT W8 2,0,2.5 x y
R RB RF
R RB RT
R RF RT
! tie the two posts together through the 3D halves, so the frame is one rigid body
R LB2 RB2
R LF2 RF2
! drive axle through both post tops, capped. The motor turns it against the frame.
R -2.828,0,2.5 2.828,0,2.5 grey
P -2.2,0,2.5 silver
P -1.8,0,2.5 silver
P 1.8,0,2.5 silver
P 2.2,0,2.5 silver
C DL D1 -2.828,0,2.5 y x
C DR D1 2.828,0,2.5 y -x
G g1 LT teeth=34
M motor LT rpm=45 torque=400
! idler axle one white rod away: exactly the 34 tooth mesh distance, so g1 drives g2
C LI W8 -2,1,3.5 x y
C RI W8 2,1,3.5 x y
R LT LI
R RT RI
R -2.828,1,3.5 2.828,1,3.5 grey
P -2.2,1,3.5 silver
P -1.8,1,3.5 silver
P 1.8,1,3.5 silver
P 2.2,1,3.5 silver
C IL D1 -2.828,1,3.5 y x
C IR D1 2.828,1,3.5 y -x
G g2 LI teeth=34
! a lever locked to the idler axle by a tan clip, and a rubber band pulling it back
H LV W8 1,1,3.5 z
P 0.8,1,3.5 silver
P 1.2,1,3.5 silver
L LV
C LVT W8 1,3,3.5 z x
R LV LVT
E band LVT RF rest=45
! a ball hanging on a string from the left post
O ball -2,-2,1.6 d=25 mass=40
Y tether LT ball
